(i) repayment is made using locally sourced IGDS (India Good Delivery Standard) / LGDS (LBMA’s Good Delivery Standards) gold;
(ii) gold is delivered on behalf of the borrower to the bank directly by the refiner or a central agency, acceptable to the bank, without the borrower’s involvement;
(iii) the loan agreement contains details of the option to be exercised by the borrower, acceptable standards and manner of delivery of gold for repayment;
(iv) the borrower is apprised upfront, in a transparent manner, of the implications of exercising the option. E. Disclosures 55A. A bank shall report the GML data to the Reserve Bank on a quarterly basis by seventh day of the following month as per the format given in Annex - V.

